    "problemStatement": "Members have no shared technology for finding common legislative interests",
    "problemDescription": "Members who share an interest in the same issue often do not know which colleagues are working on it, so bills and coalitions form through personal networks rather than through any systematic way of surfacing shared interests. The House has no technology tool built for this purpose.",
    "solutionStatement": "Offer technology tools for member collaboration on shared legislation",
    "solutionDescription": "Offer technology tools that help members find and collaborate with colleagues working on the same or related legislative issues. Members and their staff use the tools voluntarily to identify potential partners and coordinate on shared work.",
