    "problemStatement": "Committees have no guidance for setting civility norms",
    "problemDescription": "Individual committees that want to establish ground rules for how members treat each other and handle disagreement have no template or model to draw on. Chairs and ranking members who want to set a different tone must design norms from scratch, and few have the time or expertise to do so. As a result, most committees never adopt any explicit civility norms at all.",
    "solutionStatement": "Provide committees a civility norms toolkit",
    "solutionDescription": "The House develops guidance and sample language that committees can adapt to create their own tailored civility norms, covering things like speaking time, decorum, and how disputes get resolved. Adoption stays optional and each committee decides what, if anything, to put in place.",
