    "problemStatement": "Staff have no shared bipartisan workspace outside their offices",
    "problemDescription": "Staff from different offices and parties rarely interact outside of formal meetings because there is no shared physical space designed for informal, cross-office work. Existing common areas are either partisan caucus spaces or purely social, not built for staff to sit down and work alongside counterparts from other offices. The House has not tested whether shared staff workspace would change how offices collaborate.",
