    "problemStatement": "GAO does not track member and staff satisfaction with its work",
    "problemDescription": "GAO produces a large volume of reports and recommendations for Congress but has no systematic way of knowing whether members and staff are aware of what is available or satisfied with how it is delivered. Outreach happens unevenly, often depending on individual analyst relationships with particular offices. GAO cannot target its outreach investment without knowing where the gaps are.",
    "solutionStatement": "Assess and boost GAO's congressional outreach",
    "solutionDescription": "GAO expands initiatives aimed at meeting Congress's information needs and begins assessing member and staff awareness of and satisfaction with its products and services. The assessment gives GAO a basis for directing outreach where it is weakest instead of relying on existing relationships.",
    "horizonJustification": "Outreach initiatives and satisfaction surveys improve how GAO communicates but do not change its statutory role or reporting relationship, which ID 141's broader realignment would address.",
