    "problemStatement": "Constituent flag requests are tracked with no efficient process",
    "problemDescription": "Offices process requests from constituents for flags flown over the Capitol, a high volume, recurring constituent service. Without a dedicated system, staff manage requests, verify eligibility, and coordinate delivery by hand, so the process takes time disproportionate to its complexity. Each office manages it differently.",
    "solutionStatement": "Develop a shared flag request tracking process",
    "solutionDescription": "The House builds a more efficient process, potentially a shared tool, for offices to submit, track, and fulfill constituent flag requests, from intake through delivery confirmation. This frees staff time currently spent on manual tracking of a routine request type.",
    "horizonJustification": "It streamlines an existing manual workflow without changing who owns flag requests or how the underlying service is delivered.",
