    "problemStatement": "New members and staff do not know what support offices offer",
    "problemDescription": "Members and staff learn about House business support offices, such as the CAO and the Clerk, mostly by accident, through word of mouth or by stumbling into a problem the office happens to solve. There is no regular moment when those offices introduce themselves directly to a new Congress.",
    "solutionStatement": "Hold a term-start Open-House with business support offices",
    "solutionDescription": "At the start of each Congress, have House business support offices and agencies host an in-person Open-House where members and staff can meet the people and services behind each office. Offices get a direct channel to introduce what they offer before staff hit a problem that sends them looking.",
