    "problemStatement": "No record tracks how much time members spend voting late",
    "problemDescription": "Votes have an allotted time window, but the House does not publish any cumulative accounting of how much time individual members spend voting after it closes. Without a public record, there is no visible pressure on the behavior and no way to see whether it is getting better or worse.",
