    "problemStatement": "Member travel reimbursement rules do not match standard business practice",
    "problemDescription": "House rules governing travel related reimbursement for members were written separately from, and have not kept pace with, the standard business travel practices used across the private sector and the rest of the federal government. Members and their offices navigate a reimbursement process that is stricter or more confusing than the norm elsewhere, and travel expenditures are not tracked or reported in a way that supports accountability and transparency.",
    "solutionStatement": "Align member travel reimbursement with standard practice and improve transparency",
    "solutionDescription": "Rewrite House rules on member travel related expense reimbursement to match standard business travel practices used in the private sector and elsewhere in the federal government, and update travel expenditure policies to improve efficiency and strengthen accountability and transparency in how travel funds are tracked and reported. Members and offices follow the same kind of reimbursement process used everywhere else, rather than a House-specific variant.",
    "horizonJustification": "Once the rule is rewritten it applies going forward without further action or funding, so the change is durable and does not depend on any office choosing to opt in.",
