    "problemStatement": "Members and staff receive no formal debate training",
    "problemDescription": "Effective floor debate and deliberation are skills, but neither members nor staff receive structured training in them. New members learn by watching colleagues or by trial and error on the floor, and the staff who prepare talking points and debate strategy do so without formal instruction either.",
    "solutionStatement": "Debate and deliberation training for members and staff",
    "solutionDescription": "Offer voluntary training, through orientation or ongoing professional development, that teaches argumentation, rebuttal, and structured deliberation technique. Members and staff who take part bring stronger floor and committee debate skills back to their offices.",
    "horizonJustification": "Training is optional and adds a skill-building resource without changing floor rules, debate formats, or how debate time is allocated.",
