    "problemDescription": "When executive branch action affects Congress's own authority, subpoena enforcement, appropriations riders, or agency non-compliance, the House and Senate rely on small in-house counsel offices that argue those cases on top of their other duties. Courts weigh the legislative branch's arguments unevenly across cases because no consistent, adequately staffed voice represents Congress's institutional interest.",
    "solutionStatement": "Strengthen legislative branch court representation",
