    "problemStatement": "Members rarely see how other districts experience shared problems",
    "problemDescription": "Members legislate on issues, such as agriculture, manufacturing, or immigration, that play out very differently across the country, but nothing in official travel funding sends a member to see a colleague's district firsthand. Understanding of other districts comes secondhand, through hearings, staff briefings, or informal conversation rather than direct observation.",
    "solutionStatement": "Establish a district exchange travel program",
    "solutionDescription": "Let members use their Members' Representational Allowance to travel to another member's district, on a reciprocal or hosted basis, to see how a shared policy issue plays out there directly. The program runs through the existing MRA and CAO travel administration, so no new appropriation or agency is required to operate it.",
