    "problemDescription": "The Comptroller General issues a fiscal health report to the executive branch each year, but Congress has no standing annual event of its own that puts the nation's full fiscal picture, revenue, spending, and long-term obligations, before members and the public together. Fiscal debates instead happen piecemeal, bill by bill, without a shared baseline understanding of the government's financial position.",
